          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            Traditional
            %em étale cohomology
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Deligne77"} Deligne 77
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian sheaf cohomology
            for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaves
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+site"} étale site
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
            – which is an analog of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+of+open+subsets"} category of open subsets
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            , or rather the analog of the category of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+spaces"} étale spaces
            over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+set"} finite
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibers"} fibers
          %p
            A certain
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+limit"} inverse limit
            over étale cohomology groups for different
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            yields
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%E2%84%93-adic+cohomology"} ℓ-adic cohomology
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Weil+cohomology+theory"} Weil cohomology theory
          %p
            More generally, there is étale
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generalized+cohomology+theory"} generalized cohomology theory
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaves+of+spectra"} sheaves of spectra
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+site"} étale site
            (
            %a{:href => "#Jardine97"}> Jardine 97
            ). Still more generally, there is étale generalized cohomology on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-site"} étale (∞,1)-site
            (
            %a{:href => "#AntieauGepner12"}> Antieau-Gepner 12
            ,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Lurie"} Lurie
          %h2#definition Definition
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Given a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              of finite type, the small
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+site"} étale site
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi et
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{et}
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
              whose
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
              are
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+morphisms"} étale morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi R
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec R \to X
              and whose morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi R
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                    %mo :
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi R
                    %mo ′
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f:Spec R\to X)\to (f':Spec R'\to X)
              are morphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                    %mo :
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi R
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha: Spec(R)\to Spec(R')
              of schemes completing triangles:
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi α
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f'\circ\alpha=f
              (notice that the morphisms between étale morphisms are automatically étale). This category naturally carries a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+topology"} Grothendieck topology
              that makes it a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/site"} site
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+site"} étale site
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi et
                    %mo ,
                    %mi Ab
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in Sh(X_{et}, Ab)
              an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf"} abelian sheaf
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %strong étale cohomology
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mi et
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H_{et}^\bullet(X,A)
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian sheaf cohomology
              with respect to this site.
          %h2#BasicProperties Basic properties
          %p
            The following are some basic properties of étale
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohomology+groups"} cohomology groups
            for various standard choices of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
          %h3#RelationZariskiEtaleCohomology Relation to Zariski cohomology
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cover"} cover
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zariski+topology"} Zariski topology
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/schemes"} schemes
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+immersion+of+schemes"} open immersion of schemes
              and hence is in particular an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+morphism+of+schemes"} étale morphism of schemes
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+site"} étale site
              is finer than the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zariski+site"} Zariski site
              and so every étale
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
              is a Zariski sheaf, but not necessarily conversely.
          #LerayForInclusionOfZariskiIntoEtale.num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi Zar
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi et
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\epsilon \;\colon\; X_{Zar} \longrightarrow X_{et}
            %p
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zariski+site"} Zariski site
              into the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+site"} étale site
              is indeed a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/morphism+of+sites"} morphism of sites
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leray+spectral+sequence"} Leray spectral sequence
              which computes étale cohomology in terms of Zariski cohomology
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi E
                      %mn 2
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi Zar
                    %mo ,
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mi q
                    %msup
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mo *
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⇒
                    %msup
                      %mi E
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mi q
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi et
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℱ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    E^{p,q}_2 = H^p(X_{Zar}, R^q \epsilon^\ast \mathcal{F})
                    \\Rightarrow
                    E^{p+q} = H^{p+q}(X_{et}, \mathcal{F})
                    \\,.
          %p
            This is originally due to (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck"}> Grothendieck
            ,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SGA"} SGA
            4 (Chapter VII, p355)). Reviews include (
            %a{:href => "#Tamme"}> Tamme, II 1.3
            ).
          %h3#WithCoefficientsInCoherentModules With coefficients in coherent modules
          #CohomologyWithCoeffsInCoherentModules.num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-coherent+sheaf"} quasi-coherent sheaf
              of
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi et
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_{et}
              the induced étale sheaf (by the discussion at
              = succeed ")," do
                %a{:href => "etale+topos#QuasiCoherentModules"} étale topos – Quasicohetent sheaves
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/edge+morphism"} edge morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mi Zar
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mi et
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi et
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H^p_{Zar}(X, N)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    H^p_{et}(X,N_{et})
            %p
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leray+spectral+sequence"} Leray spectral sequence
              of remark
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#LerayForInclusionOfZariskiIntoEtale"}
              is an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
              for all
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian sheaf cohomology
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zariski+site"} Zariski site
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              with the étale cohomology with coefficients in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi N
                        %mi et
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_{et}
            %p
              Moreover, for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              affine we have
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi H
                      %mi et
                      %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi et
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H^p_{et}(X, N_{et}) \simeq 0
                    \\,.
          %p
            This is due to (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck"}> Grothendieck
            ,
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/FGA"} FGA
            1). See also for instance (
            %a{:href => "#Tamme"}> Tamme, II (4.1.2)
            ).
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              By the discussion at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/edge+morphism"} edge morphism
              it suffices to show that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mi q
                    %msub
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mo *
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi for
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi p
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    R^q \epsilon_\ast (N) = 0 \;\,,\;\;\; for \;\; p \gt 0
                    \\,.
            %p
              By the discussion at
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+image"} direct image
              (also at
              = succeed ")," do
                %em
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+sheaf+cohomology"} abelian sheaf cohomology
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mi q
                    %msub
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mo *
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R^q \epsilon_\ast N
              is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheaf"} sheaf
              on the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Zariski+topology"} Zariski topology
              which is the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheafification"} sheafification
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
              given by
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo ↦
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi et
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi U
                    %mo ,
                    %mi N
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    U \mapsto H^q(X_{et}|U, N)
                    \\,,
            %p
              hence it is sufficient that this vanishes, or rather, by locality (
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sheafification"}> sheafification
              ) it suffices to show this vanishes for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo =
                    %mi U
                    %mo =
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = U = Spec(A)
              an affine
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+variety"} algebraic variety
            %p
              By the existence of
              %a{:href => "etale+site#CofinalAffineCovers"} cofinal affine étale covers
              the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi X
                      %mi et
                      %mi a
                    %mo ↪
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi at
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{et}^{a} \hookrightarrow X_{at}
              with the induced
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coverage"} coverage
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+subsite"} dense subsite
              of affines. Therefore it suffices to show the statement there. Moreover, by the finiteness condition on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+morphisms"} étale morphisms
              every cover of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi X
                      %mi et
                      %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_{et}^{a}
              may be refined by a finite cover, hence by an affine covering map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Spec(B) \longrightarrow Spec(A)
                    \\,.
            %p
              It follows (by a discussion such as e.g. at
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sweedler+coring"} Sweedler coring
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cech+cohomology"} Cech cohomology
              complex
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi et
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi et
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %msup
                      %mi C
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mi et
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    N_{et}(Spec(A)) \to C^0(\{Spec(B) \to Spec(A)\}, N_{et}) \to C^1(\{Spec(B) \to Spec(A)\}, N_{et}) \to \cdots
            %p is of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo →
                    %mi N
                    %mo →
                    %mi N
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi A
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi N
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi A
                    %mi B
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi A
                    %mi B
                    %mo →
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    0 \to N \to N \otimes_A B \to N \otimes_{A} B \otimes_A B \to \cdots
                    \\,.
            %p
              known as the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Amitsur+complex"} Amitsur complex
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo →
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \to B
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/faithfully+flat+morphism"} faithfully flat morphism
              it follows by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/descent+theorem"} descent theorem
              that this is
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequence"} exact
          %h3#WithCoefficientsInACyclicGroup With coefficients in a cyclic group
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_3 Proposition
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo =
                    %mi Spec
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X = Spec(A)
              is an affine
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reduced+scheme"} reduced scheme
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic"} characteristic
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/prime+number"} prime number
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+cohomology"} étale cohomology
              with
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coefficients"} coefficients
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi p
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}
              is
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi p
                    %mi ℤ
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mrow
                      %mo {
                      %mrow
                        %mtable
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mi A
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                              %mi F
                              %mo −
                              %mi id
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mi A
                            %mtd
                              %mi if
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi q
                              %mo =
                              %mn 1
                          %mtr
                            %mtd
                              %mn 0
                            %mtd
                              %mi if
                              %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                              %mi q
                              %mo &gt;
                              %mn 0
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H^q(X, (\mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z})_X)
                    \\simeq
                    \\left\{
                    \\array{
                    A/(F - id)A &amp; if\; q = 1
                    \\\
                    0 &amp; if \; q \gt 0
                    }
                    \\right.
                    \\,.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Under the given assumptions, the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Artin-Schreier+sequence"} Artin-Schreier sequence
              (see there) induces a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequence+in+cohomology"} long exact sequence in cohomology
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mn 0
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                            %msup
                              %mi H
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi et
                            %mo ,
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi p
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo →
                            %msup
                              %mi H
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi et
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝒪
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mi F
                                %mo −
                                %mi id
                            %msup
                              %mi H
                              %mn 0
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi et
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝒪
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                            %msup
                              %mi H
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi et
                            %mo ,
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi p
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo →
                            %msup
                              %mi H
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi et
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝒪
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mi F
                                %mo −
                                %mi id
                            %msup
                              %mi H
                              %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi et
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝒪
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                            %msup
                              %mi H
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi et
                            %mo ,
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                            %mi p
                            %mi ℤ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo →
                            %msup
                              %mi H
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi et
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝒪
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mi F
                                %mo −
                                %mi id
                            %msup
                              %mi H
                              %mn 2
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %msub
                              %mi X
                              %mi et
                            %mo ,
                            %msub
                              %mi 𝒪
                              %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo →
                            %mi ⋯
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\begin{aligned}
                    0 &amp; \to
                    H^0(X_{et}, \mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}) \to H^0(X_{et}, \mathcal{O}_X) \stackrel{F-id}{\to} H^0(X_{et}, \mathcal{O}_X)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \to
                    H^1(X_{et}, \mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}) \to H^1(X_{et}, \mathcal{O}_X) \stackrel{F-id}{\to} H^1(X_{et}, \mathcal{O}_X)
                    \\\
                    \&amp; \to
                    H^2(X_{et}, \mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z}) \to H^2(X_{et}, \mathcal{O}_X) \stackrel{F-id}{\to} H^2(X_{et}, \mathcal{O}_X) \to \cdots
                    \\end{aligned}
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi F
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F(-) = (-)^p
              is the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Frobenius+endomorphism"} Frobenius endomorphism
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CohomologyWithCoeffsInCoherentModules"}
              the terms of the form
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^{p \geq 1}(X, \mathcal{O}_X)
              vanish, and so from
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exact+sequence"} exactness
              we find an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi et
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo −
                    %mi id
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi et
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi et
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi p
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    H^0(X_{et}, \mathcal{O}_X)/(F-id)(H^0(X_{et}, \mathcal{O}_X))
                    \\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                    H^1(X_{et}, \mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z})
                    \\,,
            %p hence the claimed isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi F
                    %mo −
                    %mi id
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mo ≃
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi et
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mi p
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    A/(F-id)(A)
                    \\stackrel{\simeq}{\to}
                    H^1(X_{et}, \mathbb{Z}/p\mathbb{Z})
                    \\,.
            %p By the same argument all the higher cohomology groups vanish, as claimed.
          %h3#with_coefficients_in_the_multiplicative_group With coefficients in the multiplicative group
          %p
            the étale cohomology groups with
