          %p
          %h2#section_Relation_to_motivic_cohomology Relation to motivic cohomology
          %p
            We have the following, which is Theorem 10.2 in
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#MazzaVoevodskyWeibel2006"} MazzaVoevodskyWeibel2006
          %p
          .num_theorem
            %h6 Theorem
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              be a smooth, separated
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scheme"} scheme
              over a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              be an integer prime to the characteristic of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
              and every integer
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q \geq 0
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi H
                        %mi L
                        %mrow
                          %mi p
                          %mo ,
                          %mi q
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi X
                      %mo ,
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^{p,q}_{L}(X, \mathbb{Z} / n)
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msubsup
                        %mi H
                        %mi et
                        %mi p
                      %mrow
                        %mo (
                        %mi X
                        %mo ,
                        %mi ℤ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi q
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^{p}_{et}\left(X, \mathbb{Z}/n(q) \right)
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%C3%A9tale+cohomology"} étale cohomology
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with coefficients in the
              = succeed "-th" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tate+twist"} Tate twist
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ℤ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/n
          %p
            The inverting of smashing with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tate+sphere"} Tate sphere
            as opposed to just with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{1}
            in the construction of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+motivic+homotopy+category"} stable motivic homotopy category
            allows the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            part of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/motivic+cohomology"} motivic cohomology
            to be represented in it (by the motivic Eilenberg-MacLane spectrum), as opposed to just the
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi p
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (p,0)
            part. Combining this with the above theorem, we see that inverting the Tate sphere as opposed to just
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^{1}
            allows the Tate twists of étale cohomology to be represented.
